CAT = "cdaAdvRules"; SEG = "ADV"
Q = [
("A small drone must fly 15 m from bystanders who are not part of the job. Which certificate is needed?",
 "Advanced operations", ["Basic operations", "Level 1 Complex only", "Flight reviewer rating"],
 "Flying a small RPA less than 30 m (100 ft) from uninvolved people is an advanced operation under CAR 901.62. A basic certificate covers only 30 m or more, and Level 1 Complex is for BVLOS work."),
("Under Division V, from what age may a person fly advanced operations without supervision?",
 "16", ["14", "18", "17"],
 "CAR 901.63 requires the pilot to be at least 16 and hold an advanced or Level 1 Complex certificate. Fourteen is the basic age, and 18 is the Level 1 Complex age."),
("A 15-year-old wants to fly a declared drone near people. When is that legal?",
 "Under an advanced pilot's watch", ["Holding a basic pilot certificate", "With written parental consent", "Using a declared drone on their own"],
 "CAR 901.63(2) lifts the age and certificate rule when the flight is under the direct supervision of someone permitted to fly it under Division V or VI. A basic certificate or a parent's consent does not."),
("Which two steps lead to the advanced pilot certificate?",
 "Advanced exam and flight review", ["Basic exam and logged hours", "Ground school and an SFOC", "Flight review and a declaration"],
 "CAR 901.64 issues the advanced certificate to an applicant who is 16 or older, passed the Advanced Operations examination and completed a flight review under Standard 921. No logged hours or SFOC are needed."),
("How recent must the flight review be when you apply for the advanced certificate?",
 "Within 12 months", ["Within 24 months", "Within 6 months", "Within 36 months"],
 "CAR 901.64(c) requires the flight review within the 12 months before the application. Twenty-four months is the recency period that applies after the certificate is issued."),
("Which activity counts toward the 24-month recency rule for an advanced pilot?",
 "A TC-endorsed safety seminar", ["Ten hours of logged flying", "Renewing the drone's registration", "A firmware update course"],
 "Standard 921.04 lists a Transport Canada endorsed safety seminar, a recurrent training program or the endorsed self-paced study program, and CAR 901.65 also accepts passing an exam or flight review. Flight hours do not count."),
("Which pilot may fly a Division V operation in controlled airspace?",
 "Advanced or Level 1 Complex holder", ["Basic holder, with ATC approval", "Anyone with a declared drone", "Basic holder, with an observer"],
 "CAR 901.63(1)(b) requires an advanced or Level 1 Complex pilot certificate for Division V operations. ATC approval or a declared drone does not replace the certificate."),
("Which medium-drone flight may an advanced pilot conduct under Division V?",
 "VLOS in controlled airspace", ["BVLOS over open farmland", "EVLOS in Class G", "Sheltered beside a radio tower"],
 "CAR 901.62(g) covers a medium RPA in VLOS in controlled airspace. Extended VLOS and sheltered operations under Division V are for small RPA only, and BVLOS needs Level 1 Complex."),
("Under advanced rules, which drones may fly a sheltered operation?",
 "Small RPA only", ["Medium RPA only", "Small and medium RPA", "Any RPA up to 150 kg"],
 "CAR 901.62(c) lists the sheltered operation for a small remotely piloted aircraft (250 g to 25 kg). Medium RPA under Division V are limited to VLOS."),
("Above what operating weight does a drone leave Part IX Subpart 1 and need an SFOC-RPAS?",
 "150 kg", ["25 kg", "100 kg", "250 kg"],
 "Subpart 1 covers small and medium RPA up to 150 kg. CAR 903.02 treats a drone over 150 kg as a medium-complexity SFOC application. Twenty-five kilograms is the small and medium boundary."),
("Under Part IX, what does a drone's operating weight include?",
 "Payload and safety equipment", ["Airframe and battery only", "Rated maximum take-off mass only", "Empty weight without props"],
 "CAR 900.01 defines operating weight as the weight at any point in flight, including any payload and any safety equipment on board or connected to the aircraft, such as a parachute."),
("Which certificate is needed for BVLOS flight that is neither EVLOS nor sheltered?",
 "Level 1 Complex", ["Advanced with an observer", "Advanced plus a declaration", "Flight reviewer rating"],
 "Lower-risk BVLOS operations under Division VI need the Level 1 Complex certificate. An advanced pilot can fly out of sight only in EVLOS or sheltered operations under CAR 901.74."),
("What is the minimum age for the Level 1 Complex pilot certificate?",
 "18", ["16", "17", "21"],
 "The TC AIM lists 18 years of age for the Level 1 Complex certificate, against 16 for advanced and 14 for basic."),
("How much RPAS ground school does a Level 1 Complex applicant need?",
 "20 hours", ["10 hours", "35 hours", "40 hours"],
 "The TC AIM says Level 1 Complex applicants complete 20 hours of RPAS ground school covering TP 15530 before that certificate's examination and flight review."),
("A Level 1 Complex pilot flies BVLOS under whose authority?",
 "An RPOC holder", ["A flight reviewer's rating", "An advanced SFOC", "A NAV CANADA licence"],
 "CAR 901.88 requires Level 1 Complex BVLOS flights to be flown by an RPAS operator or its employee, agent or representative, under the conditions of the RPOC."),
("A basic pilot wants to fly 3 m from a paying client with a declared drone. What is missing?",
 "Advanced certificate", ["A second visual observer", "An SFOC-RPAS", "A NOTAM for the work site"],
 "Flying a small RPA under 5 m from an uninvolved person is an advanced operation under CAR 901.62. The drone needs a 922.06 declaration and the pilot needs the advanced certificate."),
("Which flight is still a basic operation, even for an advanced pilot?",
 "Class G, 40 m from bystanders", ["Class E, 40 m from bystanders", "Class G, 20 m from bystanders", "Sheltered, beside a building"],
 "CAR 901.53 defines basic operations as small RPA in VLOS in uncontrolled airspace at least 30 m from uninvolved people. Class E is controlled, 20 m is too close, and sheltered flight is advanced."),
("Your advanced certificate was issued 30 months ago and you have done no recency activity. What applies?",
 "No flying until recent", ["Basic flights only", "Fly, and log it afterward", "Flights within 3 NM of base only"],
 "CAR 901.65 and 901.56 both need recency within the preceding 24 months, so no Part IX operation is allowed until the pilot completes an exam, flight review or recurrent training activity."),
("You completed TC's self-paced recency program. Where is the completed copy kept?",
 "With the pilot", ["Sent to Transport Canada", "Filed with the flight school", "Uploaded to NAV Drone"],
 "The TC AIM says the completed self-paced study program is kept by the pilot and must be easily accessible during operations. It does not need to be sent to Transport Canada."),
("Which pilot may fly an EVLOS operation in Class G airspace?",
 "Advanced certificate holder", ["Basic certificate holder", "Uncertified, with an observer", "Any registered drone owner"],
 "CAR 901.62(b) puts extended VLOS operations in Division V, so the pilot needs the advanced or Level 1 Complex certificate. A basic certificate holder may act as the visual observer but not the pilot."),
]
